      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "USB sheet: 'J17 USB_C_Receptacle_USB2.0' ... 'D+ A6' -- R12 5.1k -- NET00126, 'D- A7' -- R66 5.1k -- NET00134"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "USB Serial sheet: R83 27R / R82 27R in series with FT231XS USBDM/USBDP"}
      ],
      "impact": "The USB data pair between the USB-C connector and the CM4 would be severely attenuated/blocked, so USB device/host operation over J17 would fail or be unreliable.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design is largely consistent with the specification (16 MHz MCP2515 crystals, 75R Bob-Smith Ethernet terminations, 120R CAN terminations, LTC4412 ideal-diode path, e-stop buffers), but the USB-C data pair appears to carry 5.1k series resistors (R66/R12) instead of the small (0-27R) series value required, which would break the USB link; confidence is limited because the value/pin association at J17 is small in the drawing."
